From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Mendyka <jkmendyka@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:41:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] mcd_panel: always run the panel init sequence in the
 kernel

The rev2 bootloader hands over the rm69091 panel in sleep-in with TE
off. The driver trusted the bootloader state (NORMAL), skipped the init
sequence, and decon panicked on the vsync timeout at the first frame.
Treat a bootloader-initialized panel as powered but not initialized.
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/mcd_panel/panel_drv.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/mcd_panel/panel_drv.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/mcd_panel/panel_drv.c
index 9094957b4..895bf254e 100755
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/mcd_panel/panel_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/mcd_panel/panel_drv.c
@@ -3181,9 +3181,16 @@ int panel_drv_set_gpios(struct panel_device *panel)
 		 */
 		panel_info("ub connected\n");
 		panel->state.connect_panel = PANEL_CONNECT;
-		panel_set_cur_state(panel, PANEL_STATE_NORMAL);
+		/*
+		 * Do not trust the panel state left by the bootloader: the rev2
+		 * bootloader (R870XXS2JZG3) hands over a panel in sleep-in with
+		 * TE off, so the kernel never gets a vsync. Mark the panel as
+		 * powered but not initialized, so the first sleep-out runs the
+		 * full init sequence (TE on, sleep out, display on).
+		 */
+		panel_set_cur_state(panel, PANEL_STATE_ON);
 		panel->state.power = PANEL_POWER_ON;
-		panel->state.disp_on = PANEL_DISPLAY_ON;
+		panel->state.disp_on = PANEL_DISPLAY_OFF;
 		gpio_direction_output(gpio[PANEL_GPIO_RESET].num, 1);
 	} else {
 		panel_info("ub disconnected\n");
